169-class StreamingDataset(Array, IterableDataset):
170-    """A mid-epoch-resumable streaming/caching pytorch IterableDataset.
171-
172-    Features elastically deterministic shuffling, which enables fast mid-epoch resumption.
173-
174-    Checkpoints are represented in JSON as follows:
175-
176-    .. code-block:: json
177-
178-        {
179-            "epoch" :"int",
180-            "sample_in_epoch": "int",
181:            "shuffle_seed": "int",
182-            "num_canonical_nodes": "int"
183-        }
184-
185-    StreamingDataset init takes two kinds of arguments:
186-
187-    * What to iterate:
188-
189-      * One or more streams (you must provide either ``streams`` or ``remote``/``local``):
190-
191-        * ``streams``
192-        * ``remote``
193-        * ``local``
194-
195-      * Knobs to control streaming behavior, which, if multiple streams are provided,
196-        become defaults applied to each of them:
197-
198-        * ``split``
199-        * ``download_retry``
200-        * ``download_timeout``
201-        * ``validate_hash``
202-        * ``keep_zip``
203-
204-      * Absolute dataset size, if streams were weighted relatively:
205-
206-        * ``epoch_size``
207-
208-    * How to iterate:
209-
210-      * Shard lifecycle:
211-
212-        * ``predownload``
213-        * ``cache_limit``
214-
215-      * Sampling:
216-
217-        * ``sampling_method``
218-        * ``sampling_granularity``
219-
220-      * Determinism:
221-
222-        * ``partition_algo``
223-        * ``num_canonical_nodes``
224-        * ``batch_size``
225-
226-      * Shuffling:
227-
228:        * ``shuffle``
229:        * ``shuffle_algo``
230:        * ``shuffle_seed``
231:        * ``shuffle_block_size``
232-
233-      * Batching:
234-
235-        * ``batching_method``
236-
237-
238-    Args:
239-        streams (Sequence[Stream], optional): One or more streams to stream/cache samples from,
240-            which may be upsampled or downsampled. StreamingDataset uses either ``streams`` or
241-            ``remote``/``local``. Defaults to ``None``.
242-        remote (str, optional): Remote path or directory to download the dataset from. If ``None``,
243-            its data must exist locally. StreamingDataset uses either ``streams`` or
244-            ``remote``/``local``. Defaults to ``None``.
245-        local (str, optional): Local working directory to download shards to. This is where shards
246-            are cached while they are being used. Uses a temp directory if not set.
247-            StreamingDataset uses either ``streams`` or ``remote``/``local``. Defaults to ``None``.
248-        split (str, optional): Which dataset split to use, if any. If provided, we stream from/to
249-            the ``split`` subdirs of  ``remote`` and ``local``. Defaults to ``None``.
250-        download_retry (int): Number of download re-attempts before giving up. Defaults to ``2``.
251-        download_timeout (float): Number of seconds to wait for a shard to download before raising
252-            an exception. Defaults to ``60``.
253-        validate_hash (str, optional): Optional hash or checksum algorithm to use to validate
254-            shards. Defaults to ``None``.
255-        keep_zip (bool): Whether to keep or delete the compressed form when decompressing
256-            downloaded shards. If ``False``, keep iff remote is local or no remote. Defaults to
257-            ``False``.
258-        epoch_size (Union[int, str], optional): Number of samples to draw per epoch balanced
259-            across all streams. If ``None``, takes its value from the total number of underlying
260-            samples. Provide this field if you are weighting streams relatively to target a larger
261-            or smaller epoch size. Defaults to ``None``. Can also take in human-readable number
262-            abbreviations (e.g., ``"100k"``, ``"64M"``, ``"77b"``, etc). Defaults to ``None``.
263-        predownload (int, optional): Target number of samples to download per worker in advance
264-            of current sample. Workers will attempt to download ahead by this many samples during,
265-            but not before, training. Recommendation is to provide a value greater than per device
266-            batch size to ensure at-least per device batch size number of samples cached locally.
267-            If ``None``, its value is set to ``8 * batch_size``. Defaults to ``None``.
268-        cache_limit (Union[int, str], optional): Maximum size in bytes of this StreamingDataset's
269-            shard cache. Before downloading a shard, the least recently used resident shard(s)
270-            may be evicted (deleted from the local cache) in order to stay under the limit.
271-            Set to ``None`` to disable shard eviction. Supports integer bytes as well as string
272-            human-readable bytes (e.g., ``100b``, ``64kb``, ``77mb``, and so on). Defaults to
273-            ``None``.
274-        sampling_method (str): Which sampling method to use, either ``balanced`` or ``fixed``.
275-            Defaults to ``balanced``.
276-        sampling_granularity (int): When picking samples for a stream's final partial repeat,
277-            how many samples to pick from the same shard at a time (``1`` for evenly balanced
278-            across shards, ``1000`` to pick 1000 samples from the same shard at a time, etc).
279-            Defaults to ``1``.
280-        partition_algo (str): Which partitioning algorithm to use. Defaults to ``relaxed``.
281-        num_canonical_nodes (int, optional): Canonical number of nodes for shuffling with
282-            resumption. The sample space is divided evenly according to the number of canonical
283-            nodes. The higher the value, the more independent non-overlapping paths the
284-            StreamingDataset replicas take through the shards per model replica (increasing data
285-            source diversity). If ``None``, this is interpreted as 64 times the number of physical
286:            nodes of the initial run if ``shuffle_algo`` is ``py1s`` or ``py2s``, and simply the
287-            number of physical nodes of the initial run otherwise. Defaults to ``None``.
288-
289-            .. note::
290-
291:                For sequential sample ordering, set ``shuffle`` to ``False`` and
292-                ``num_canonical_nodes`` to the number of physical nodes of the initial run.
293-        batch_size (int, optional): Per-device batch size, the same as what is passed to the
294-            DataLoader. This affects how the dataset is partitioned over the workers and is
295-            necessary for deterministic resumption and optimal performance. Defaults to ``None``.
296:        shuffle (bool): Whether to iterate over the samples in randomized order. Defaults to
297-            ``False``.
298:        shuffle_algo (str): Which shuffling algorithm to use. Defaults to ``py1e``.
299:        shuffle_seed (int): Seed for deterministic data shuffling. Defaults to ``9176``.
300:        shuffle_block_size (int, optional): Unit of shuffle. A canonical node's samples are split
301:            into blocks of this size, and samples within each block are shuffled. If ``None``, its
302-            value is calculated as ``max(4_000_000 // num_canonical_nodes), 1 << 18)``. Defaults to
303-            ``None``.
304-        batching_method (str): Which batching method to use, either ``random``, ``stratified``,
305-            ``per_stream``, or ``device_per_stream``. Defaults to ``random``.
306-        allow_unsafe_types (bool): If a shard contains Pickle, which allows arbitrary code
307-            execution during deserialization, whether to keep going if ``True`` or raise an error
308-            if ``False``. Defaults to ``False``.
309-        replication (int, optional): Determines how many consecutive devices will receive the same
310-            samples. Useful for training with tensor or sequence parallelism, where multiple
311-            devices need to see the same partition of the dataset. Defaults to ``None``.
312-        stream_name (str): The name of the Stream to use which is registered in streams_registry.
313-            Defaults to ``stream``.
314-        stream_config (dict[str, Any]): Additional arguments to pass to the Stream constructor.
315-    """
