.1d">1 ≤ italic_t ≤ italic_T</annotation></semantics></math>. By doing so, we assume the partition for buffers and mini-batches to be fixed throughout the training procedure. Under the above linear regression setup, we can express the gradient and Hessian matrix of the least square
296:loss explicitly. Thus, the updating formula (<a class="ltx_ref" href="#S2.Ex1" title="2.2 Buffered mini-batch gradient descent ‣ 2 Methodology"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>) can be rewritten as:</p>
